<title>CHINA: HK's Tung drives home warning to property punters.</title>
<headline>HK's Tung drives home warning to property punters.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong's new leader Tung Chee-hwa said on Wednesday his administration might take measures to clamp down on property speculation, which has driven home prices to astronomical levels.</p>
<p>&quot;Speculation has been damaging. It cannot be tolerated. We have been studying this closely,&quot; he said in his first news conference since Hong Kong's return to China on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;If necessary, we will act. There are some ways we can do it,&quot; he told reporters. He refused to say what measures might be taken.</p>
<p>It was the second time in two days that Tung has warned about action to curb property speculation.</p>
</text>
